    "id": "i2",
    "kind": "Javadoc",
    "lines": [
     84,
     91
    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Tests for {@link JulianChronology} and {@link JulianDate}. <p>The Julian calendar drifts from ISO because it applies a leap year every 4 years without exception (unlike Gregorian which skips century years not divisible by 400). Julian 0001-01-01 aligns to ISO 0000-12-30, so every Julian date is offset from its ISO equivalent by the accumulated drift."
   },
